# UI (tview) conventions

- Central type is `UI` in `app.go`. Wire keys in `input`; keep footer/README shortcuts in sync.
- Async HTTP: send on a goroutine, deliver via `results` channel, drain in `BeforeDraw`/`receive`. One request at a time; `cancel` for Ctrl+X.
- Dirty tracking: compare editor draft to `baseline`; confirm before quit/load when unsaved.
- Layout: sidebar list when wide enough; narrow terminals use F2 full-width list (see `layout`).
- Environments: modal flows in `environments.go`; Escape backs out of dialogs.
- Do not enable tview dynamic colors on response/status text (`SafeText` strips controls).
- Prefer small methods on `*UI` over new packages unless the surface grows substantially.
- After UX changes, extend `app_test.go` where logic is testable without a real terminal.
